	1.	Start the flow
The process starts when the Jira import test case calls JiraIntegration.jiraImport(), which delegates the orchestration to JiraFlowCoordinator.
	2.	Execute the automation suite
The business test suite runs normally and generates the Katalon report structure, JUnit result, execution logs, and runtime artifacts.
	3.	Register visible report steps
During execution, step by step tests explicitly call JiraReportSteps.note('...') to create the business readable steps that will later appear in the custom HTML report.
	4.	Capture evidence when needed
During execution, JiraImagesEvidence can save controlled screenshots manually, and it can also generate automatic failure evidence when a test fails.
	5.	Collect runtime report metadata
The ematchReport listener tracks start time, end time, duration, report step markers, failure summary, and runtime metadata needed by the custom report.
	6.	Resolve the correct report folder
JiraFlowCoordinator locates the correct execution report folder, avoiding collection and Jira import folders that should not be used as the main source.
	7.	Detect the suite and find the XML result file
The suite name is extracted from the report structure, and the flow locates the JUnit_Report.xml file that will be imported into Jira.
	8.	Build the custom eMatch HTML report
JiraReportBuilder prepares the normalized report model using XML, listener traces, visible steps, timings, failures, and evidences, then JiraHtmlTemplateBuilder renders the final HTML report.
	9.	Resolve or create the Test Plan
JiraTestPlanManager checks whether the current suite should reuse an existing Test Plan or create a new one, using Jira searches and saved key validation.
	10.	Import execution results into Jira
JiraExecutionPublisher, through JiraGateway, imports the XML result file into Jira so the Test Execution is created.
	11.	Link the execution to the Test Plan
After the execution is created, the integration adds it to the resolved Test Plan.
	12.	Update execution metadata
The integration updates execution fields such as summary, labels, and environment to match the current run.
	13.	Package execution artifacts
JiraExecutionPublisher creates the ZIP files for results and evidences, following the current packaging and exclusion rules.
	14.	Upload attachments
The generated custom HTML report, Results.zip, and Evidences.zip are uploaded to the Jira Test Execution.
	15.	Finish the Jira publishing flow
At the end, the execution is fully published with XML results, metadata, report, and evidence attached in Jira.
